cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use phylokit-mcp in your work, please cite it as below. IQ-TREE 2 is the
  inference engine this server drives and must be cited separately — see
  references.
title: phylokit-mcp
abstract: >-
  A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for phylogenetic inference, driving
  IQ-TREE 2 through piqtree. It enforces one structural rule: a topology without
  support is not a result. Tree inference always runs a bootstrap and always
  returns per-clade support, with no flag to skip it. Threads are pinned before
  the engine is imported, because likelihood sums accumulate in a
  thread-dependent order and unpinned runs are not reproducible.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Arnold
    given-names: Jaret
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-4055-5238"
repository-code: "https://github.com/musharna/phylokit-mcp"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/phylokit-mcp/"
license: GPL-2.0-only
version: 0.2.2
date-released: "2026-07-31"
keywords:
  - phylogenetics
  - iqtree
  - bootstrap
  - maximum-likelihood
  - bioinformatics
  - model-context-protocol
  - mcp
references:
  - type: article
    title: "IQ-TREE 2: New Models and Efficient Methods for Phylogenetic Inference in the Genomic Era"
    authors:
      - family-names: Minh
        given-names: Bui Quang
      - family-names: Schmidt
        given-names: Heiko A.
      - family-names: Chernomor
        given-names: Olga
